KG42.register("nodes-b8c222f3ebf8af96bb515ca1",{"id":"COMP-ffbf050cce03a2e6","code":"OMC010","label":"Matching of local purchase and sale orders","definition":"In local electricity trading, pair the buy orders and sell orders submitted by participants according to market rules, and determine the transaction relationship between the corresponding buyers and sellers.","layer":"L4","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"matching.counterparties","concept_ids":["matching.counterparties"],"identity_dimensions":{"definition":"In local electricity trading, pair the buy orders and sell orders submitted by participants according to market rules, and determine the transaction relationship between the corresponding buyers and sellers.","object":"Electricity purchase and sale orders for the corresponding trading period and their trading entities.","inputs":"Includes two-sided orders containing trading entities, requested or offered electricity quantities, and prices, as well as the matching rules specified by the source.","operation":"Select executable combinations from buy and sell orders and establish explicit counterparty relationships.","outputs":"Successfully matched purchaser-seller combinations.","boundary":"Limited to counterparty selection in L4 and DA; quantity allocation, price formation, and payment are retained separately. CDA's trigger, price-time priority, and termination rules are not extrapolated as common conditions of BMG."},"exclusions":[["Distinguish the general C4 matching definition from the specific BMG implementation; BMG uses a closed order book and a discrete double auction in 15-minute periods.","Orders contain electricity quantity and price; the consumer's maximum price, the prosumer's minimum selling price, and the allocation order described by the source are retained, and a complete CDA ordering rule is not presumed.","The market mechanism is carried by smart contracts, and payment is executed after matching is completed; payment is a use of the matching result.","Retain the illustrated C_1→P_24 and C_5→P_22, the x_clearing on the arrows, and the min{y_1,y_24} and min{y_5,y_22} below them; these are not independent pair-selection algorithms or payment-amount equations."],["Within the Agreement Period, each target period is matched independently; both new buy orders and new sell orders can trigger matching.","Buy prices in descending order, sell prices in ascending order, with first-arrival priority at the same price; proceeding downward from the top of the order book and stopping when matching cannot continue.","Retain π_{b,t}≥π_{s,t}⇒σ_{matched,t}=min(σ_{b,t},σ_{s,t}); order prices are in £/kWh and quantities are in kWh.","For the corresponding buyer and seller, establish an 〈σ_{matched,t},π_t〉 agreement; prior matching results can be used by ZIP to adjust quotes, and this feedback use is not included in the common matching definition."]],"members":[{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Submitted buy orders provide requested quantities and bid prices to local clearing, which allocates the highest bidder first and then lower bidders. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Submitted sell orders provide offered quantities and prices to the market mechanism responsible for local energy allocation. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Matching participants' buy and sell orders is specified as the means of achieving efficient local energy allocation. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price receive additional energy allocated through a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. Scope: BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers Condition: Consumers do not undercut the clearing price. Minimum and maximum energy-allocation constraints should exist, especially to account for prosumer generation constraints. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Different market time horizons should ideally be implemented, and allocation mechanisms must be tailored to achieve efficient allocation at each stage. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons Local energy allocation should preferably operate at near-real-time granularity. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Local clearing uses a closed order book and a time-discrete double auction in 15-minute slots. Scope: BMG specified double-auction mechanism","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers | BMG specified double-auction mechanism | BMG specified local double-auction mechanism | General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons | General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e35"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"1bbe8c3fe342874c6a3359fb3aba730cc3386f72459200ac03dd4f4c78b1f84b","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004","node_id":"matching.counterparties","function":"matching.counterparties","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"Submitted buy orders, which include requested quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders. Submitted sell orders, which include offered quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002"],"decision_anchor":"matching.counterparties","source_rule_sha256":"c4f0c1af6d959f2b68c5affe530b95e4549a3e0ed788b3b905b49daea356f33b","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007","node_id":"matching.counterparties","function":"matching.counterparties","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","market_meaning":"Local allocation supplies the allocated participants between whom financial transactions are carried out according to predefined payment rules. Scope: BMG virtual-market financial transactions between allocated participants. The local transaction price determined by the pricing mechanism is used for monetary payment; the illustrated BMG payment rules use the clearing price. Scope: Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules. Payment is carried out once counterparty matching is completed. Scope: BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. Condition: Matching has been completed. Consumers pay their producing neighbors for feeding renewable generation into the distribution grid. Scope: Physical-layer interpretation of BMG virtual-market payments. Condition: Producing neighbors feed renewable generation into the distribution grid.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. | BMG virtual-market financial transactions between allocated participants. | Physical-layer interpretation of BMG virtual-market payments. | Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e35","v141-b-g03-e022"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C005"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"cbcdd5e0a18793905b4452d98d282abe6114cf83dee8226cbc4b4d7be776a3c1","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012","node_id":"matching.counterparties","function":"matching.counterparties","unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R005::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"Results of preceding bid/ask matching provide feedback for customers' ZIP bid/ask price adjustments. Scope: Customers' decentralized ZIP price decisions during the CDA Agreement Period. The successful CDA trading price provides the comparison reference for customers' subsequent ZIP bid/ask price decisions. Scope: ZIP price decisions for bids and asks remaining in the order book for time slot t. Condition: The last CDA matching was successfully made at price π_t. In this successful-matching branch, arrival of an ask conditions the downward ZIP revision of an eligible bid price toward the feed-in tariff reference. Scope: ZIP revisions of bid prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. Condition: The last matching was successful and π_{b,t} \u003c= π_t at the corresponding test in the update sequence. In the unsuccessful-matching branch, arrival of an ask conditions downward ZIP revisions of ask prices toward the feed-in tariff reference. Scope: ZIP revisions of ask prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. Condition: The last matching was unsuccessful. In this successful-matching branch, arrival of a bid conditions the downward ZIP revision of an eligible ask price toward the feed-in tariff reference. Scope: ZIP revisions of ask prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. Condition: The last matching was successful and π_{s,t} >= π_t at the corresponding test in the update sequence. In the unsuccessful-matching branch, arrival of a bid conditions downward ZIP revisions of bid prices toward the feed-in tariff reference. Scope: ZIP revisions of bid prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. Condition: The last matching was unsuccessful.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Customers' decentralized ZIP price decisions during the CDA Agreement Period. | ZIP price decisions for bids and asks remaining in the order book for time slot t. | ZIP revisions of ask prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. | ZIP revisions of bid prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g04-E04"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"4f9ba33d76e97791c04081906953d99fb7e8b35773708528b2af2647fbfc281d","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R005","node_id":"matching.counterparties","function":"matching.counterparties","unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::matching.counterparties","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","anchor":false},{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"The counterparty-matching process is triggered whenever a newly submitted demand bid arrives at the exchange. Scope: Counterparty matching in the community CDA during its Agreement Period, within the corresponding time-slot order book. Condition: Arrival of a new buyer bid; this is an alternative trigger to arrival of a new seller ask. The counterparty-matching process is triggered whenever a newly submitted supply ask arrives at the exchange. Scope: Counterparty matching in the community CDA during its Agreement Period, within the corresponding time-slot order book. Condition: Arrival of a new seller ask; this is an alternative trigger to arrival of a new buyer bid. The community exchange performs counterparty matching by attempting to match the bids and asks in the order book. Scope: The exchange coordinating P2P energy trading within the community, for each corresponding CDA order book. Condition: A bid or ask arrives and is placed in the corresponding order book. The CDA matches the candidate buyer and seller when the bid price is at least the ask price, establishing their P2P trading agreement for the matched electricity. Scope: Candidate buyer bids and seller asks considered in the corresponding community CDA order book. Condition: The candidate bid and ask satisfy π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}. Matching proceeds from the top to the bottom of the order book and stops when no further match can be made. Bids rank by descending bid price and asks by ascending ask price; among equal-priced orders, later arrivals rank lower. Scope: Counterparty matching within each time-slot order book of the community CDA.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"Candidate buyer bids and seller asks considered in the corresponding community CDA order book. | Counterparty matching in the community CDA during its Agreement Period, within the corresponding time-slot order book. | Counterparty matching within each time-slot order book of the community CDA. | The exchange coordinating P2P energy trading within the community, for each corresponding CDA order book.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005"],"decision_anchor":"matching.counterparties","source_rule_sha256":"7e8c24a4511f9ed33e0b2edfc84c14d9f58268282cd9443d38a9c6231250c6ff","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006","node_id":"matching.counterparties","function":"matching.counterparties","unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::matching.counterparties","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["24-brooklyn_microgrid","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Market mechanism (C4)","anchor_text":"( ) The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employable bidding language and a clearly defined bidding format [50]. The market mechanism is implemented by the information system (C3). Its main objective is to provide an efficient allocation of the traded energy by matching the market participants’ buy and sell orders [31]. This should best be done in (near) real time granularity [31].","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","quote":"The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employable bidding language and a clearly defined bidding format [50]. The market mechanism is implemented by the information system (C3). Its main objective is to provide an efficient allocation of the traded energy by matching the market participants’ buy and sell orders [31]. This should best be done in (near) real time granularity [31]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Market mechanism (C4)","anchor_text":"( ) The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employable bidding language and a clearly defined bidding format [50]. The market mechanism is implemented by the information system (C3). Its main objective is to provide an efficient allocation of the traded energy by matching the market participants’ buy and sell orders [31]. This should best be done in (near) real time granularity [31].","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employable bidding language and a clearly defined bidding format [50]. The market mechanism is implemented by the information system (C3). Its main objective is to provide an efficient allocation of the traded energy by matching the market participants’ buy and sell orders [31]. This should best be done in (near) real time granularity [31]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26].","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e30","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 3","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the pricing mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the order book would be matched. The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU).","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the order book would be matched. The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e35","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1 Project overview","anchor_text":"g remaining power. The physical microgrid currently comprises ens 10-by-10 housing blocks and will b","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Buy and ask orders are created according to this information, and orders are send to the market mechanism (C4) that is sustained by a smart contract. Once the matching is completed, payment is carried out and a new block (here Block iv) is added to the blockchain. This block includes all current market information. The required information (i.e. conducted transactions) is also send to the involved agents via their blockchain accounts.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"Buy and ask orders are created according to this information, and orders are send to the market mechanism (C4) that is sustained by a smart contract. Once the matching is completed, payment is carried out and a new block (here Block iv) is added to the blockchain. This block includes all current market information. The required information (i.e. conducted transactions) is also send to the involved agents via their blockchain accounts."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e35","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1 Project overview","anchor_text":"g remaining power. The physical microgrid currently comprises ens 10-by-10 housing blocks and will b","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Buy and ask orders are created according to this information, and orders are send to the market mechanism (C4) that is sustained by a smart contract. Once the matching is completed, payment is carried out and a new block (here Block iv) is added to the blockchain. This block includes all current market information. The required information (i.e. conducted transactions) is also send to the involved agents via their blockchain accounts.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"Buy and ask orders are created according to this information, and orders are send to the market mechanism (C4) that is sustained by a smart contract. Once the matching is completed, payment is carried out and a new block (here Block iv) is added to the blockchain. This block includes all current market information. The required information (i.e. conducted transactions) is also send to the involved agents via their blockchain accounts."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"C4: Payment rules: $C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24}$; $C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}$.","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"C4: Payment rules: $C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24}$; $C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e021","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Sell Orders: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); Buy Order: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); x_clearing","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","quote":"Sell Orders: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); Buy Order: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); x_clearing"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. > 0. Similarly, tothe amount of electricity to be bought being NL*i,t, if NL*i,t the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The bid/ask prices are assumed to be made given the assumption that the customers act as ‘zero intelligent plus (ZIP)’ traders [41]. The assumption of ZIP traders can well mimic the behaviors of human traders in stock markets. As a ZIP trader, each customer will set a budget constraint, [p_t^{FiT}, p_t^{retail}] to ensure that it will not be worse off by participating in the P2P energy trading compared to trading with the power utility. Initially, for each customer, the price for its bid/ask is decided uniformly at random within the budget constraint. During the double auction process, the customers will dynamically adjust their bid/ask prices based on matching results of previous bids/asks.","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","quote":"The bid/ask prices are assumed to be made given the assumption that the customers act as ‘zero intelligent plus (ZIP)’ traders [41]. The assumption of ZIP traders can well mimic the behaviors of human traders in stock markets. As a ZIP trader, each customer will set a budget constraint, [p_t^{FiT}, p_t^{retail}] to ensure that it will not be worse off by participating in the P2P energy trading compared to trading with the power utility. Initially, for each customer, the price for its bid/ask is decided uniformly at random within the budget constraint. During the double auction process, the customers will dynamically adjust their bid/ask prices based on matching results of previous bids/asks."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The matching process will go from the top to the bottom of the order book, and will end once no matching can be made. The matching process will be triggered every time a new bid/ask arrives.","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"The matching process will go from the top to the bottom of the order book, and will end once no matching can be made. The matching process will be triggered every time a new bid/ask arrives."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 2. The timeline for ancillary service provision As presented in Section 2, customers trade ener","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A bid, which is submitted by a buyer, is represented by o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}), which means that the buyer b_t would like to by the σ_{b,t} (kWh) amount of electricity at the price π_{b,t} (£/kWh), and the bid arrives at the ‘exchange’ at the time τ_{b,t}. Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community. Similarly, an ask, which is submitted by a seller is represented by o_{s,t}(s_t, π_{s,t}, σ_{s,t}, τ_{s,t}).","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"A bid, which is submitted by a buyer, is represented by o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}), which means that the buyer b_t would like to by the σ_{b,t} (kWh) amount of electricity at the price π_{b,t} (£/kWh), and the bid arrives at the ‘exchange’ at the time τ_{b,t}. Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community. Similarly, an ask, which is submitted by a seller is represented by o_{s,t}(s_t, π_{s,t}, σ_{s,t}, τ_{s,t})."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"provision from a P2P energy trading community. to (£/kWh), a P2P energy trading agreement, \u003cσmatched","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"When an amount of demand and generation, σ_{matched,t} (kWh), is matched at the price π_t (£/kWh), a P2P energy trading agreement, \u003cσ_{matched,t}, π_t>, is established between the corresponding buyer and seller, specifying the quantity and price to be traded.","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"When an amount of demand and generation, σ_{matched,t} (kWh), is matched at the price π_t (£/kWh), a P2P energy trading agreement, \u003cσ_{matched,t}, π_t>, is established between the corresponding buyer and seller, specifying the quantity and price to be traded."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E06","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Within the Agreement Period of CDA, bids and asks will arrive at the exchange asynchronously. After they arrive, the bids and asks are allocated in ‘order books’. Note that for the bids and asks associated with each time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In each order book, the bids are sorted in the descending order of the bid prices π_{b,t} and the asks are sorted in the ascending order of the ask prices π_{s,t}. For both bids and asks, if several ones have the same prices, they are sorted based on the arrival time - the later a bid/ask arrives, the lower it ranks.","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Within the Agreement Period of CDA, bids and asks will arrive at the exchange asynchronously. After they arrive, the bids and asks are allocated in ‘order books’. Note that for the bids and asks associated with each time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In each order book, the bids are sorted in the descending order of the bid prices π_{b,t} and the asks are sorted in the ascending order of the ask prices π_{s,t}. For both bids and asks, if several ones have the same prices, they are sorted based on the arrival time - the later a bid/ask arrives, the lower it ranks."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["buy_sell_order_counterparty_matching","price_time_priority_counterparty_matching"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L4-7dfc6fb527","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L4","ontological_kind":"buy_sell_order_counterparty_matching"},"semantic_definition":{"definition":"In local electricity trading, pair the buy orders and sell orders submitted by participants according to market rules, and determine the transaction relationship between the corresponding buyers and sellers.","object":"Electricity purchase and sale orders for the corresponding trading period and their trading entities.","inputs":"Includes two-sided orders containing trading entities, requested or offered electricity quantities, and prices, as well as the matching rules specified by the source.","operation":"Select executable combinations from buy and sell orders and establish explicit counterparty relationships.","outputs":"Successfully matched purchaser-seller combinations.","boundary":"Limited to counterparty selection in L4 and DA; quantity allocation, price formation, and payment are retained separately. CDA's trigger, price-time priority, and termination rules are not extrapolated as common conditions of BMG."},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","paper_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"matching.counterparties","source_occurrences":[{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","market_meaning":"Submitted buy orders provide requested quantities and bid prices to local clearing, which allocates the highest bidder first and then lower bidders. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Submitted sell orders provide offered quantities and prices to the market mechanism responsible for local energy allocation. Scope: BMG specified local double-auction mechanism Matching participants' buy and sell orders is specified as the means of achieving efficient local energy allocation. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price receive additional energy allocated through a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. Scope: BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers Condition: Consumers do not undercut the clearing price. Minimum and maximum energy-allocation constraints should exist, especially to account for prosumer generation constraints. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Different market time horizons should ideally be implemented, and allocation mechanisms must be tailored to achieve efficient allocation at each stage. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons Local energy allocation should preferably operate at near-real-time granularity. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4 Local clearing uses a closed order book and a time-discrete double auction in 15-minute slots. Scope: BMG specified double-auction mechanism","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"BMG allocation of additional hyper-local or traditional energy sources to consumers | BMG specified double-auction mechanism | BMG specified local double-auction mechanism | General microgrid market-mechanism design across electricity-market time horizons | General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e35"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"1bbe8c3fe342874c6a3359fb3aba730cc3386f72459200ac03dd4f4c78b1f84b"},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"Submitted buy orders, which include requested quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders. Submitted sell orders, which include offered quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002"],"decision_anchor":"matching.counterparties","source_rule_sha256":"c4f0c1af6d959f2b68c5affe530b95e4549a3e0ed788b3b905b49daea356f33b"},{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R012","market_meaning":"Local allocation supplies the allocated participants between whom financial transactions are carried out according to predefined payment rules. Scope: BMG virtual-market financial transactions between allocated participants. The local transaction price determined by the pricing mechanism is used for monetary payment; the illustrated BMG payment rules use the clearing price. Scope: Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules. Payment is carried out once counterparty matching is completed. Scope: BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. Condition: Matching has been completed. Consumers pay their producing neighbors for feeding renewable generation into the distribution grid. Scope: Physical-layer interpretation of BMG virtual-market payments. Condition: Producing neighbors feed renewable generation into the distribution grid.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. | BMG virtual-market financial transactions between allocated participants. | Physical-layer interpretation of BMG virtual-market payments. | Schematic local order-book transactions and the illustrated BMG payment rules.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e35","v141-b-g03-e022"]},"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C005"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"cbcdd5e0a18793905b4452d98d282abe6114cf83dee8226cbc4b4d7be776a3c1"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Matching participants' buy and sell orders is specified as the means of achieving efficient local energy allocation. Scope: General microgrid market-mechanism design, component C4","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e09"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R004","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Market mechanism (C4)","anchor_text":"( ) The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employable bidding language and a clearly defined bidding format [50]. The market mechanism is implemented by the information system (C3). Its main objective is to provide an efficient allocation of the traded energy by matching the market participants’ buy and sell orders [31]. This should best be done in (near) real time granularity [31]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted buy orders, which include requested quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e35"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Market mechanism (C4)","anchor_text":"( ) The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employable bidding language and a clearly defined bidding format [50]. The market mechanism is implemented by the information system (C3). Its main objective is to provide an efficient allocation of the traded energy by matching the market participants’ buy and sell orders [31]. This should best be done in (near) real time granularity [31]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e30","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 3","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the pricing mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the order book would be matched. The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e35","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1 Project overview","anchor_text":"g remaining power. The physical microgrid currently comprises ens 10-by-10 housing blocks and will b","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Buy and ask orders are created according to this information, and orders are send to the market mechanism (C4) that is sustained by a smart contract. Once the matching is completed, payment is carried out and a new block (here Block iv) is added to the blockchain. This block includes all current market information. The required information (i.e. conducted transactions) is also send to the involved agents via their blockchain accounts."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted sell orders, which include offered quantities, provide inputs to counterparty matching. Scope: C4 microgrid energy-market design: matching participants’ buy and sell orders.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e35"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":"g pp y g ensured without the traditional grid. The BMG’s market mechanism is implemented on the Tran","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Any prosumer $P_g$ and consumer $C_a$ willing to trade electricity in the next time slot, can submit buy or sell orders via their EMTS (C6) to the market. Any order includes an order quantity and price. The market mechanism (C4) is a closed order book with a time discrete double auction in 15 min time slots. For now, consumers constantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable energy). Prosumers bid the minimum price limit that they request for selling their generation on the microgrid market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Market mechanism (C4)","anchor_text":"( ) The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market mechanism comprises the market’s allocation and payment rules, and provides an employable bidding language and a clearly defined bidding format [50]. The market mechanism is implemented by the information system (C3). Its main objective is to provide an efficient allocation of the traded energy by matching the market participants’ buy and sell orders [31]. This should best be done in (near) real time granularity [31]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Similar to a merit-order dispatch, the highest bidder is allocated first, then the lower bidders are allocated. The last allocated bid price represents the market clearing price for this time slot (C5). Consumers that do not undercut the clearing price will be supplied by additional energy sources (i.e. hyper-local energy or traditional “brown” energy) allocated over a similar bidding mechanism or predefined prices. This is well in line with the market mechanism presented by Ilic et al. [26]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e30","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-matching","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 3","anchor_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the pricing mec","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 3. A schematic overview of the seven market components. The upper two orders in the order book would be matched. The transaction price will be determined by the pricing mechanism and paid in monetary units (MU)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e35","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1 Project overview","anchor_text":"g remaining power. The physical microgrid currently comprises ens 10-by-10 housing blocks and will b","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Buy and ask orders are created according to this information, and orders are send to the market mechanism (C4) that is sustained by a smart contract. Once the matching is completed, payment is carried out and a new block (here Block iv) is added to the blockchain. This block includes all current market information. The required information (i.e. conducted transactions) is also send to the involved agents via their blockchain accounts."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C003","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Payment is carried out once counterparty matching is completed. Scope: BMG smart-contract market transaction workflow. Condition: Matching has been completed.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e35"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e35","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.1 Project overview","anchor_text":"g remaining power. The physical microgrid currently comprises ens 10-by-10 housing blocks and will b","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Buy and ask orders are created according to this information, and orders are send to the market mechanism (C4) that is sustained by a smart contract. Once the matching is completed, payment is carried out and a new block (here Block iv) is added to the blockchain. This block includes all current market information. The required information (i.e. conducted transactions) is also send to the involved agents via their blockchain accounts."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"In the illustrated BMG payment rules, consumer C1 is annotated as paying producer P24 and consumer C5 as paying producer P22, with the clearing price x_clearing shown above the arrow and the allocated quantity min{y_1,y_24} or min{y_5,y_22} shown below the arrow. The source presents this arrow annotation rather than a separately written payment-amount equation.","expression":"C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24};\\quad C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","matching.counterparties","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_x_clearing","theta_y_consumer","theta_y_producer"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2 Market mechanism","anchor_text":", stantly bid their maximum price limit for their preferred energy sources (e.g. local renewable ene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"For example, consumer $C_1$ bids a maximum price $x_1$ for quantity $y_1$, prosumer $P_{24}$ offers quantity $y_{24}$ for a minimum price of $x_{24}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"C4: Payment rules: $C_1 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_1,y_{24}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{24}$; $C_5 \\xrightarrow[\\min\\{y_5,y_{22}\\}]{x_{\\text{clearing}}} P_{22}$."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-e021","location":{"location_id":"src-d1d75d8eed-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"Fig. 6","anchor_text":"Fig. 6. A schematic representation of local electricity transactions conducted in the BM employment ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Sell Orders: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); Buy Order: Price (MU/kWh), Quantity (kWh); x_clearing"}]}],"variables":[],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"theta_x_clearing","symbol":"x_{\\text{clearing}}","meaning":"Clearing price for the time slot used as the transaction price in the illustrated BMG payment-rule annotation. The quoted payment annotation does not give a separate formula for how the clearing price is determined.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"x_{\\text{clearing}}"},"unit":"MU/kWh","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::theta::theta_x_clearing"},{"parameter_id":"theta_y_consumer","symbol":"y_i","meaning":"Order quantity submitted by a consumer i, used in the payment annotation's allocated quantity min{y_i,y_j}; the source presents y_1 and y_5 as instances.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"y_i"},"unit":"kWh","indices":["i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::theta::theta_y_consumer"},{"parameter_id":"theta_y_producer","symbol":"y_j","meaning":"Order quantity offered by a prosumer j, used in the payment annotation's allocated quantity min{y_i,y_j}; the source presents y_24 and y_22 as instances.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"y_j"},"unit":"kWh","indices":["j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R012","declaration_ref":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::theta::theta_y_producer"}]},{"unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::matching.counterparties","paper_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","function":"matching.counterparties","source_occurrences":[{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R005::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R005","market_meaning":"Results of preceding bid/ask matching provide feedback for customers' ZIP bid/ask price adjustments. Scope: Customers' decentralized ZIP price decisions during the CDA Agreement Period. The successful CDA trading price provides the comparison reference for customers' subsequent ZIP bid/ask price decisions. Scope: ZIP price decisions for bids and asks remaining in the order book for time slot t. Condition: The last CDA matching was successfully made at price π_t. In this successful-matching branch, arrival of an ask conditions the downward ZIP revision of an eligible bid price toward the feed-in tariff reference. Scope: ZIP revisions of bid prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. Condition: The last matching was successful and π_{b,t} \u003c= π_t at the corresponding test in the update sequence. In the unsuccessful-matching branch, arrival of an ask conditions downward ZIP revisions of ask prices toward the feed-in tariff reference. Scope: ZIP revisions of ask prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. Condition: The last matching was unsuccessful. In this successful-matching branch, arrival of a bid conditions the downward ZIP revision of an eligible ask price toward the feed-in tariff reference. Scope: ZIP revisions of ask prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. Condition: The last matching was successful and π_{s,t} >= π_t at the corresponding test in the update sequence. In the unsuccessful-matching branch, arrival of a bid conditions downward ZIP revisions of bid prices toward the feed-in tariff reference. Scope: ZIP revisions of bid prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. Condition: The last matching was unsuccessful.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Customers' decentralized ZIP price decisions during the CDA Agreement Period. | ZIP price decisions for bids and asks remaining in the order book for time slot t. | ZIP revisions of ask prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period. | ZIP revisions of bid prices in order book t during the CDA Agreement Period.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15","v141-b-g04-E04"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"4f9ba33d76e97791c04081906953d99fb7e8b35773708528b2af2647fbfc281d"},{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::V::matching.counterparties","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"The counterparty-matching process is triggered whenever a newly submitted demand bid arrives at the exchange. Scope: Counterparty matching in the community CDA during its Agreement Period, within the corresponding time-slot order book. Condition: Arrival of a new buyer bid; this is an alternative trigger to arrival of a new seller ask. The counterparty-matching process is triggered whenever a newly submitted supply ask arrives at the exchange. Scope: Counterparty matching in the community CDA during its Agreement Period, within the corresponding time-slot order book. Condition: Arrival of a new seller ask; this is an alternative trigger to arrival of a new buyer bid. The community exchange performs counterparty matching by attempting to match the bids and asks in the order book. Scope: The exchange coordinating P2P energy trading within the community, for each corresponding CDA order book. Condition: A bid or ask arrives and is placed in the corresponding order book. The CDA matches the candidate buyer and seller when the bid price is at least the ask price, establishing their P2P trading agreement for the matched electricity. Scope: Candidate buyer bids and seller asks considered in the corresponding community CDA order book. Condition: The candidate bid and ask satisfy π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}. Matching proceeds from the top to the bottom of the order book and stops when no further match can be made. Bids rank by descending bid price and asks by ascending ask price; among equal-priced orders, later arrivals rank lower. Scope: Counterparty matching within each time-slot order book of the community CDA.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"Candidate buyer bids and seller asks considered in the corresponding community CDA order book. | Counterparty matching in the community CDA during its Agreement Period, within the corresponding time-slot order book. | Counterparty matching within each time-slot order book of the community CDA. | The exchange coordinating P2P energy trading within the community, for each corresponding CDA order book.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11"]},"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005"],"decision_anchor":"matching.counterparties","source_rule_sha256":"7e8c24a4511f9ed33e0b2edfc84c14d9f58268282cd9443d38a9c6231250c6ff"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Results of preceding bid/ask matching provide feedback for customers' ZIP bid/ask price adjustments. Scope: Customers' decentralized ZIP price decisions during the CDA Agreement Period.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E15"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R005","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E15","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p05-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. > 0. Similarly, tothe amount of electricity to be bought being NL*i,t, if NL*i,t the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The bid/ask prices are assumed to be made given the assumption that the customers act as ‘zero intelligent plus (ZIP)’ traders [41]. The assumption of ZIP traders can well mimic the behaviors of human traders in stock markets. As a ZIP trader, each customer will set a budget constraint, [p_t^{FiT}, p_t^{retail}] to ensure that it will not be worse off by participating in the P2P energy trading compared to trading with the power utility. Initially, for each customer, the price for its bid/ask is decided uniformly at random within the budget constraint. During the double auction process, the customers will dynamically adjust their bid/ask prices based on matching results of previous bids/asks."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The counterparty-matching process is triggered whenever a newly submitted demand bid arrives at the exchange. Scope: Counterparty matching in the community CDA during its Agreement Period, within the corresponding time-slot order book. Condition: Arrival of a new buyer bid; this is an alternative trigger to arrival of a new seller ask.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The matching process will go from the top to the bottom of the order book, and will end once no matching can be made. The matching process will be triggered every time a new bid/ask arrives."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The counterparty-matching process is triggered whenever a newly submitted supply ask arrives at the exchange. Scope: Counterparty matching in the community CDA during its Agreement Period, within the corresponding time-slot order book. Condition: Arrival of a new seller ask; this is an alternative trigger to arrival of a new buyer bid.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The matching process will go from the top to the bottom of the order book, and will end once no matching can be made. The matching process will be triggered every time a new bid/ask arrives."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The community exchange performs counterparty matching by attempting to match the bids and asks in the order book. Scope: The exchange coordinating P2P energy trading within the community, for each corresponding CDA order book. Condition: A bid or ask arrives and is placed in the corresponding order book.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 2. The timeline for ancillary service provision As presented in Section 2, customers trade ener","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A bid, which is submitted by a buyer, is represented by o_{b,t}(b_t, π_{b,t}, σ_{b,t}, τ_{b,t}), which means that the buyer b_t would like to by the σ_{b,t} (kWh) amount of electricity at the price π_{b,t} (£/kWh), and the bid arrives at the ‘exchange’ at the time τ_{b,t}. Note that the exchange is a centralized or decentralized platform set for P2P energy trading within the community. Similarly, an ask, which is submitted by a seller is represented by o_{s,t}(s_t, π_{s,t}, σ_{s,t}, τ_{s,t})."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The CDA matches the candidate buyer and seller when the bid price is at least the ask price, establishing their P2P trading agreement for the matched electricity. Scope: Candidate buyer bids and seller asks considered in the corresponding community CDA order book. Condition: The candidate bid and ask satisfy π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}.","expression":"π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t} ⇒ σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t})","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":["x-v141-c-R006-pi-b","x-v141-c-R006-sigma-b","x-v141-c-R006-pi-s","x-v141-c-R006-sigma-s","x-v141-c-R006-sigma-matched"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E11"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E07","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Every time a bid/ask arrives at the exchange, it will be allocated in the corresponding order book based on the above-described principles, and then the exchange will try to match the bids and asks in the order book. If the following relationship is satisfied for a bid o_{b,t} and an ask o_{s,t}: π_{b,t} ≥ π_{s,t}, (1) then the following amount of electricity will be matched: σ_{matched,t} = min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}) (2)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"provision from a P2P energy trading community. to (£/kWh), a P2P energy trading agreement, \u003cσmatched","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"When an amount of demand and generation, σ_{matched,t} (kWh), is matched at the price π_t (£/kWh), a P2P energy trading agreement, \u003cσ_{matched,t}, π_t>, is established between the corresponding buyer and seller, specifying the quantity and price to be traded."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Matching proceeds from the top to the bottom of the order book and stops when no further match can be made. Bids rank by descending bid price and asks by ascending ask price; among equal-priced orders, later arrivals rank lower. Scope: Counterparty matching within each time-slot order book of the community CDA.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E10"],"ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E06","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"peach time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In seeach order book, the bi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Within the Agreement Period of CDA, bids and asks will arrive at the exchange asynchronously. After they arrive, the bids and asks are allocated in ‘order books’. Note that for the bids and asks associated with each time slot t in the Target Time Period T, there is one order book. In each order book, the bids are sorted in the descending order of the bid prices π_{b,t} and the asks are sorted in the ascending order of the ask prices π_{s,t}. For both bids and asks, if several ones have the same prices, they are sorted based on the arrival time - the later a bid/ask arrives, the lower it ranks."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E10","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-matching","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The bid/ask that is fully matched will be removed from the order pr book, and the bid/ask that is no","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The matching process will go from the top to the bottom of the order book, and will end once no matching can be made. The matching process will be triggered every time a new bid/ask arrives."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"x-v141-c-R006-pi-b","symbol":"π_{b,t}","meaning":"Bid price of demand bid o_{b,t} for time slot t in the CDA order book.","kind":"operational","domain":"Price in £/kWh carried by a demand bid; source defines it as the bid price and states no separate numerical bound in the matching rule.","unit":"£/kWh","indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-pi-b"},{"variable_id":"x-v141-c-R006-sigma-b","symbol":"σ_{b,t}","meaning":"Electricity amount requested by demand bid o_{b,t} for time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Order quantity in kWh; source defines it as the amount of electricity the buyer would like to buy.","unit":"kWh","indices":["b","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-sigma-b"},{"variable_id":"x-v141-c-R006-pi-s","symbol":"π_{s,t}","meaning":"Ask price of supply ask o_{s,t} for time slot t in the CDA order book.","kind":"operational","domain":"Price in £/kWh carried by a supply ask; source defines it as the ask price and states no separate numerical bound in the matching rule.","unit":"£/kWh","indices":["s","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-pi-s"},{"variable_id":"x-v141-c-R006-sigma-s","symbol":"σ_{s,t}","meaning":"Electricity amount offered by supply ask o_{s,t} for time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Order quantity in kWh; source defines it as the amount of electricity the seller would like to sell.","unit":"kWh","indices":["s","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-sigma-s"},{"variable_id":"x-v141-c-R006-sigma-matched","symbol":"σ_{matched,t}","meaning":"Matched electricity amount for a compatible bid-ask pair in time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Matched quantity in kWh defined by the source as min(σ_{b,t}, σ_{s,t}); no independent bound is stated.","unit":"kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","declaration_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::x::x-v141-c-R006-sigma-matched"}],"parameters":[]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","stage":"L4","subtype":"buy_sell_order_counterparty_matching","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"The market mechanism receives buy and sell orders and performs pairing to determine the two trading parties; the pairing result provides the counterparties required for subsequent payment.","form_kind":"procedural","identity_fields":["Object: buy and sell orders and their participating entities","Operation: match buy orders with sell orders","Output: explicit counterparty combinations"],"variation_fields":["Orders contain requested or offered electricity quantities","BMG carries the market mechanism through smart contracts","The illustrated trading pairs are C_1 with P_24 and C_5 with P_22","Completion of matching is a precondition for subsequent payment"],"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C005"],"paper_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"matching.counterparties","template_code":"DA"},{"unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::matching.counterparties","stage":"L4","subtype":"price_time_priority_counterparty_matching","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"Arrival of a new buy or sell order triggers matching: buy orders by descending price and sell orders by ascending price, with first-arrival priority at the same price; proceeding downward from the top of the order book, determine trading pairs for orders satisfying π_{b,t}≥π_{s,t} until matching cannot continue.","form_kind":"procedural","identity_fields":["Object: buy-side and sell-side orders within the same order book","Core operation: select trading pairs according to price-time priority and price-compatibility conditions","Output: the buyer and seller establishing a P2P trading agreement"],"variation_fields":["Each target period is matched independently, executed by the community exchange","Arrival of either buy orders or sell orders can trigger","The agreement records the traded quantity and traded price; the matching result can then be used for ZIP feedback"],"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005"],"paper_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01-p2p-cda","function":"matching.counterparties","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[{"unit_id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","source_definition":"The market mechanism receives buy and sell orders and performs pairing to determine the two trading parties; the pairing result provides the counterparties required for subsequent payment.","retained_variants":["Distinguish the general C4 matching definition from the specific BMG implementation; BMG uses a closed order book and a discrete double auction in 15-minute periods.","Orders contain electricity quantity and price; the consumer's maximum price, the prosumer's minimum selling price, and the allocation order described by the source are retained, and a complete CDA ordering rule is not presumed.","The market mechanism is carried by smart contracts, and payment is executed after matching is completed; payment is a use of the matching result.","Retain the illustrated C_1→P_24 and C_5→P_22, the x_clearing on the arrows, and the min{y_1,y_24} and min{y_5,y_22} below them; these are not independent pair-selection algorithms or payment-amount equations."],"constraint_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004::v141-c-R004-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012::v141-c-R012-C005"]},{"unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M01-p2p-cda::matching.counterparties","source_definition":"Arrival of a new buy or sell order triggers matching: buy orders by descending price and sell orders by ascending price, with first-arrival priority at the same price; proceeding downward from the top of the order book, determine trading pairs for orders satisfying π_{b,t}≥π_{s,t} until matching cannot continue.","retained_variants":["Within the Agreement Period, each target period is matched independently; both new buy orders and new sell orders can trigger matching.","Buy prices in descending order, sell prices in ascending order, with first-arrival priority at the same price; proceeding downward from the top of the order book and stopping when matching cannot continue.","Retain π_{b,t}≥π_{s,t}⇒σ_{matched,t}=min(σ_{b,t},σ_{s,t}); order prices are in £/kWh and quantities are in kWh.","For the corresponding buyer and seller, establish an 〈σ_{matched,t},π_t〉 agreement; prior matching results can be used by ZIP to adjust quotes, and this feedback use is not included in the common matching definition."],"constraint_refs":["25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R005::v141-c-R005-C001"]}],"source_parent_definition":{"definition":"In local electricity trading, pair the buy orders and sell orders submitted by participants according to market rules, and determine the transaction relationship between the corresponding buyers and sellers.","object":"Electricity purchase and sale orders for the corresponding trading period and their trading entities.","inputs":"Includes two-sided orders containing trading entities, requested or offered electricity quantities, and prices, as well as the matching rules specified by the source.","operation":"Select executable combinations from buy and sell orders and establish explicit counterparty relationships.","outputs":"Successfully matched purchaser-seller combinations.","boundary":"Limited to counterparty selection in L4 and DA; quantity allocation, price formation, and payment are retained separately. CDA's trigger, price-time priority, and termination rules are not extrapolated as common conditions of BMG."},"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/300"});
